    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows a downward trend (e.g., dropping from ~79 to ~75), failing to account for immediate volatility.",
    "Forecasts systematically overshoot true outcomes by 10-15 EUR during the first 3-5 days of the 30-day horizon, creating a false sense of stability before a sharp reversal occurs.",
    "Sentiment spikes (values > 0.20) in the last 3 days of history correlate with model overconfidence; true outcomes often reverse direction immediately after these sentiment peaks.",
    "Model fails to capture mean reversion dynamics, predicting a slow linear recovery from lows while actual prices exhibit high-frequency oscillations between 65 and 80 EUR.",
    "When recent history ends near local minima (e.g., 75.10), the model predicts a gradual climb, whereas true outcomes frequently drop further before recovering."
